I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to another  edition of ask Evan today maintain a  question from one of our Facebook fans  on the Telus talks business Facebook  page John Carter who wrote insane I have  a question for Evan comic com for the  challenge series for growing real estate  investment business what are the  employee roles we should hire as we grow  we currently have an outsourced model  with marketing web design property  management legal accounting and  bookkeeping outsourced so thanks for the  question John congrats and building the  business up to that size so far I'm  going to give you three pieces advice  that I hope will help you take your  business to the next step number one  what score do your business before you  outsource anything in your business you  should ask yourself which functions are  core to what you do and which are  supportive for example bookkeeping and  accounting makes sense to outsource your  real estate company not an accounting  firm let them do what they do best so  you can do more of what you do best  other areas like marketing can be  trickier is your marketing methodology a  key component to your company is that a  differentiating factor compared your  competition is it core to the way you do  business vital to your success if no  then outsource if yes then keep it  in-house as you building your business  think of it as an asset that you're  eventually going to sell and for a great  price too if your marketing process is  indeed core to your success then keeping  it internally increases the value of  your asset you can't leverage outsourced  bookkeeping for example to sell your  business for a higher price outsourcing  is a fantastic way to let other people  do what score to them and let you do  what score to you before you outsource  your next function think about what  really makes your company successful and  what's going to boost your growth over  the next five years anything that is a  key component to that success should be  made core and kept in-house  number two where do you add the most  value just because a function is core to  your company success it doesn't mean  that you have to do it next up is to  think about what is core to you yes it's  time to give up control it's easy to  give away the tasks you're not good at  and don't enjoy but you'll often have to  give up some projects that you do enjoy  and are the best at because your time  can be put to better use somewhere else  where do you add the most value to your  business the more time you spend on  those high-value activities the more  your business is going to grow the other  tasks still have to get done but they  can be handled by someone on your team  I'm constantly asking myself from the  way to the office what can I do today  that will add the most value to my  business if you find yourself doing too  many repetitive or low value tasks to  think about elimination automation and  delegation number three make room for  CEO time my final piece of advice is to  make sure you spend time on your  business and not just in it this is what  I call CEO time if you're constantly  being dragged back into the day-to-day  operations of your business then you  won't be able to spend any time growing  it when you're first starting out you  have to get past the survival stage  where you have enough money to put food  on the table and pay the bills after  that it's time to think about growth and  it won't come with you trying to do  everything yourself make sure you've  blocked out time every week ideally  every day where people know not to  distract you so you can have your CEO  time to focus on growth projects for  most entrepreneurs is easiest to have  their CEO time in the morning before the  craziness of the day hits as much as  possible I try to build a no crisis  business where we can focus on being  proactive and chasing down new  opportunities instead of constantly  reacting to emergencies and putting out  fires you get there by controlling your  time and setting boundaries around what  you will and will not accept you have to  first appreciate and recognize that your  time is extremely valuable before others  will  thank you for joining me for another  edition of ask Evan if you like the  video you wanted some more please give  it a thumbs up below it makes you want  to do more of these videos for you and  if you have a question about this video  or question about your own business I  feel free to leave in the comments  section below or join us in the facebook  conversation and hopefully we can  feature you in the next challenge series  video that we do for Telus talks  business  you
 

